16a. Welcomes the fact that the Clean Industrial Deal provides for a revision of the Public Procurement Directive1a with the aim of mainstreaming the use of non-price criteria in accordance with the EU’s strategic goals; reiterates the need for clear and mandatory social and sustainability criteria to be included in the Public Procurement Directive to ensure that European industry workers benefit from any public support provided to industry; underlines that this also includes criteria ensuring that all workers have collective bargaining rights;

---

1a Directive 2014/24/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 February 2014 on public procurement and repealing Directive 2004/18/EC (*OJ L 94, 28.3.2014, p. 65, *ELI:[http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2014/24/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2014/24/oj)).
